### Variables
# Set WEBHOOK_SECRET to match your .env value
# The signature below was computed with secret = "dev-secret-changeme"
# To recompute: node -e "console.log('sha256='+require('crypto').createHmac('sha256','dev-secret-changeme').update('<body>').digest('hex'))"

### Local — Normal webhook (202 + background processing)
POST http://localhost:8080/webhook/github
Content-Type: application/json
X-GitHub-Event: issue_comment
X-GitHub-Delivery: manual-test-001
X-Hub-Signature-256: sha256=c0f969df5772715afaf2801c42edf54a4deb0cd17c4b21e6a5e71aba0656708e

{
  "action": "created",
  "repository": {
    "full_name": "gugacarbo/user-request-issue-writter",
    "name": "user-request-issue-writter",
    "owner": { "login": "gugacarbo" }
  },
  "issue": {
    "number": 1,
    "title": "Test issue",
    "body": "This is a test issue"
  },
  "comment": {
    "body": "Please create an issue to investigate the login flow in src/index.ts",
    "user": { "login": "tester" },
    "html_url": "https://github.com/gugacarbo/user-request-issue-writter/issues/1#issuecomment-1"
  }
}

### Local — DryRun (200 + JSON with drafted issue, no createIssue)
POST http://localhost:8080/webhook/github?dryRun=true
Content-Type: application/json
X-GitHub-Event: issue_comment
X-GitHub-Delivery: manual-test-002
X-Hub-Signature-256: sha256=c0f969df5772715afaf2801c42edf54a4deb0cd17c4b21e6a5e71aba0656708e

